    {
      "id": "floating-forward-for-answers",
      "title": "Floating Forward For Answers",
      "title_from_manifest": true,
      "group": "painting",
      "year": "2026",
      "medium": "Acrylic on timber",
      "edition": "1/1",
      "image": "https://assets.mintface.art/recent/floating-forward-for-answers.jpg",
      "aspect": 2.0408,
      "orientation": "landscape",
      "pricing_nzd": {
        "digital": null,
        "painting": 1500,
        "both": 1500
      },
      "added": "2026-08-17T00:04:00.000Z",
      "dimensions": {
        "w": 120,
        "h": 60,
        "d": 1,
        "unit": "cm"
      },
      "notes": null,
      "updated": "2026-08-18T00:00:32.729Z",
      "statement": "A floral mass untethered from ground, drifting across a chalky white field with that lime halo spinning above like a benevolent sun or a question mark redrawn as orbit. The paint handling is closer to Twombly's late Peony panels than anything else here: fat, wristy blossom-marks that stay marks, never tipping into illustration, with the white doing as much work as the colour. But where Twombly's peonies sink downward with haiku melancholy, this bouquet floats up and forward, weightless, the drift itself the point. \n\nThe title confirms it... not answers arrived at, just the willingness to move toward them, painted as levitation.\n\nThere's a lightness of spirit here that reads as hard-won rather than naive... the empty white isn't absence, it's permission."
    },
