    {
      "id": "striving-upward",
      "title": "Striving Upward",
      "title_from_manifest": true,
      "group": "painting",
      "year": "2026",
      "medium": "Acrylic on timber",
      "edition": "1/1",
      "image": "https://assets.mintface.art/recent/striving-upward.jpg",
      "aspect": 2.0322,
      "orientation": "landscape",
      "pricing_nzd": {
        "digital": null,
        "painting": 3000,
        "both": 3000
      },
      "added": "2026-08-17T00:13:00.000Z",
      "statement": "pure kinetics... the trunks aren't trees so much as a single continuous gesture looping across the canvas, closer to Twombly's Bacchus loops than anything botanical, but where Bacchus was blood-drunk and circular, this is lateral, wind-driven, insistently alive. The canopies land as calligraphic knots, the sun almost an afterthought... the real subject is momentum, growth as handwriting. There's Hockney in the optimism and van Gogh's cypresses in the torque, but the arabesque doing all the structural work is the signature move.\n\nIn the MintFace canon it pairs naturally with Cycle of Silence as its answer... same looping energy, but the vortex uncoiled and set running. Silence spins inward, this one strives outward. Hung together they'd read as trap and release.",
      "dimensions": {
        "w": 120,
        "h": 60,
        "d": 1,
        "unit": "cm"
      },
      "notes": null,
      "updated": "2026-08-17T23:56:33.557Z"
    },
