      "notes": null,
      "updated": "2026-08-17T23:58:36.036Z",
      "statement": "Dissolved-garden register where foliage and light lose their edges. With it, the whole surface becomes somatic: the greens curdle, the drips at the base read as internal bleeding, the scrubbed and scratched-back passages feel like walking through beauty while something fails inside you. \n\nIt's closest to Twombly's Green Paintings in spirit... nature as veil over distress... but Mitchell is the truer kin, the way she made landscape carry grief without depicting it."
    },
